AU  - Garg, Jugal
AU  - Sharma, Eklavya
AU  - Taki, Setareh
PY  - 2024
T2  - Proceedings of the 25th ACM Conference on Economics and Computation
AB  - We consider fair division of a set of indivisible goods among n agents with additive valuations using the fairness notion of maximin share (MMS). MMS is the most popular share-based notion, in which an agent finds an allocation fair to her if she receives goods worth at least her (1-out-of-n) MMS value. An allocation is called MMS if all agents receive their MMS values. However, since MMS allocations do not always exist [Kurokawa et al., JACM'18], the focus shifted to investigating its ordinal and multiplicative approximations.
